 ell explicitly uses 23:59 AoE and requires a two-page paper\, video\, and
  interactive demonstration. The Feb 16 update is not a fresh submission r
 oute. XL reflects the official description of more than 2\,000 annual att
 endees\; the ICORE rank and historical acceptance fields describe the mai
 n conference\, not its demonstration track.\nScope: Speech science and sp
 eech technology\, linking spoken-language research with computational met
 hods for speech recognition\, speech synthesis\, and speech communication
 . Machine learning and language models are relevant through speech and sp
 oken-language problems. The current 2027 overview emphasizes the relation
 ship between speech research and spoken-language technologies.\nAdditiona
 l topics: \nScope sources (2027): https://interspeech2027.org/\nScope las
 t checked: 2026-10-07\nOfficial deadline day\; exact cutoff hour/timezone
  is unannounced. Verify the organizer's submission portal.
